I doubdt it.  SRM is probably looking at the manufacturer/device
IDs in the PCI config on the card and comparing to its own
built-in table, and not finding it.  I'm not sure it's easy (or
possible -- possibly a checksum would be wrong) to binary patch
the SRM firmware (not for the faint of heart!) to force it into
recognizing the card and use it as an 53c810.

> FYI, the Tekram DC-310 card, with the 53c810AE chipset probes
> as follows in NetBSD:
>
> ncr0 at pci0 dev 9 function 0: ncr 53c810a fast10 scsi

That doesn't tell the PCI manufacturer/device IDs; you need a
kernel with PCIVERBOSE (I think).

