From root@garbled.net  Sun Aug 22 08:41:26 1999
From: Tim Rightnour <root@garbled.net>
To: shsrms@erols.com
Date: Sun, 22 Aug 1999 08:41:26 +0000
Subject: RE: Another Dumb Question?: PCI PNP modem in a Multia.

On 22-Aug-99 Sheila&bob/Herbal Gypsy and the Tinker wrote:
> I have this Plug and pray PCI 56K modem.

I have never seen a PCI modem that wasn't a winmodem.

The fact that it says plug and play isn't really relevant..  all PCI is what
microsoft refers to as plug and play.. the actual PNP "spec" is only relevant
on ISA.  (They also refer to monitors as PNP, which confuses the heck out of me)

NetBSD may detect your modem.. but I would be truly amazed if it wasn't a
winmodem and thus useless.

